WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.222 --> 00:00:02.639
- I'm so happy for you right now!

00:00:02.639 --> 00:00:04.220
(mumbling)

00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:06.660
(laughing)

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:07.640
- Hi, I'm Gena.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.630
I'm here with actor, Michael Ward,

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:11.480
who plays Jamie on Top Boy

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:13.368
and these are his Netflix nine!

00:00:13.368 --> 00:00:15.210
(upbeat music)

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:16.720
- Not only have you joined

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:19.476
the cast of critically acclaimed show,

00:00:19.476 --> 00:00:22.910
it's been executive produced

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:24.308
by Drake.

00:00:24.308 --> 00:00:25.141
- Drizzy!

00:00:25.141 --> 00:00:26.040
- What was it like meeting

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:27.320
and working with him?

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:28.837
- Yeah, like, the weirdest thing about me

00:00:28.837 --> 00:00:29.845
meeting him was that

00:00:29.845 --> 00:00:31.150
I actually watched him at Wireless

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:31.983
the day before.

00:00:31.983 --> 00:00:33.057
So I see, like,

00:00:33.057 --> 00:00:34.470
two big security guards come,

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:35.710
looking left and right.

00:00:35.710 --> 00:00:36.690
Drake comes through

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:38.025
and I'm just standing there, like,

00:00:38.025 --> 00:00:39.522
trying to not make it bait.

00:00:39.522 --> 00:00:40.511
Oh my god!

00:00:40.511 --> 00:00:42.620
That was one of the
baddest things, actually!

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:43.470
Then Drake just came over

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:44.580
and giving me a hug

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:45.413
and saying, "You all right?"

00:00:45.413 --> 00:00:46.594
And I was like, "Yeah!"

00:00:46.594 --> 00:00:47.446
You know what I'm saying?

00:00:47.446 --> 00:00:48.279
I was (mumbles).

00:00:48.279 --> 00:00:49.123
- How did you keep it?

00:00:49.123 --> 00:00:49.956
I would be like,

00:00:49.956 --> 00:00:51.120
"I'm fine! No idea who
you are, by the way."

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:52.550
- No , but I'm actor.

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:54.130
We can pretend to be cool.

00:00:54.130 --> 00:00:54.963
- No, you're right.

00:00:54.963 --> 00:00:55.796
- You know what I'm saying?

00:00:55.796 --> 00:00:56.629
So I was acting cool.

00:00:56.629 --> 00:00:58.211
As soon as he went inside

00:00:58.211 --> 00:01:00.403
(laughs)

00:01:00.403 --> 00:01:01.820
Yeah, it was mad!

00:01:03.059 --> 00:01:03.892
(Drake) Yeah!

00:01:03.892 --> 00:01:04.933
- Let them know, man!

00:01:04.933 --> 00:01:06.068
Let them know what we about!

00:01:06.068 --> 00:01:07.570
Aye yo!

00:01:07.570 --> 00:01:08.816
- Do you guys have each other

00:01:08.816 --> 00:01:10.100
on Instagram or stuff?

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:12.039
- Not yet. Not yet but soon.

00:01:12.039 --> 00:01:12.878
I'm guessing.

00:01:12.878 --> 00:01:13.711
- I was going to be like,

00:01:13.711 --> 00:01:14.570
can you just message him

00:01:14.570 --> 00:01:15.403
and be like I met this girl

00:01:15.403 --> 00:01:16.444
called Gena.

00:01:16.444 --> 00:01:17.277
- You say,

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:18.260
with the plug he's out here!

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:19.166
Six years ago

00:01:19.166 --> 00:01:21.220
you tweeted that you couldn't wait

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:22.270
for Top Boy to come around.

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:23.103
- Oh, you saw that?

00:01:23.103 --> 00:01:23.936
- I saw that tweet because

00:01:23.936 --> 00:01:24.769
I do my research.

00:01:24.769 --> 00:01:27.073
Because I'm a very good interviewer!

00:01:27.073 --> 00:01:28.237
You tweeted that

00:01:28.237 --> 00:01:30.200
and now you're starring in it.

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:31.200
- It's crazy!

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:32.122
- What's it like coming into something

00:01:32.122 --> 00:01:33.940
that's so important to people?

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:36.040
Like, Top Boy is such a
big thing to come into.

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:38.842
- It's a big, big, big blessing,

00:01:38.842 --> 00:01:40.640
first and foremost.

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:43.340
And being able to act alongside

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:44.830
people I've seen on screen

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:46.282
six, seven, well eight years ago

00:01:46.282 --> 00:01:47.480
is when it was made,

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:48.331
isn't it?

00:01:48.331 --> 00:01:49.164
- And what was your reaction

00:01:49.164 --> 00:01:50.874
when you got the role?

00:01:50.874 --> 00:01:52.510
- I was actually in Glasgow,

00:01:52.510 --> 00:01:53.720
in Maru, by myself

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:55.306
and I knew I was going to get a call.

00:01:55.306 --> 00:01:56.139
So, it was like,

00:01:56.139 --> 00:01:57.920
I can't get this call around people

00:01:57.920 --> 00:01:59.660
so I was constantly just trying to

00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:00.920
run back to the room

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:01.753
or whatever.

00:02:01.753 --> 00:02:02.586
And as soon as soon as

00:02:02.586 --> 00:02:03.419
I go back to the room

00:02:03.419 --> 00:02:04.252
I was like, yo, call me now!

00:02:04.252 --> 00:02:06.333
And then, yeah, Red D to the call

00:02:06.333 --> 00:02:08.080
and it was just a big lead up.

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:10.885
And then Rei, the first director,

00:02:10.885 --> 00:02:12.381
He called me and said

00:02:12.381 --> 00:02:14.897
how would I like to take Top Boy three?

00:02:14.897 --> 00:02:15.909
I was like, "What?

00:02:15.909 --> 00:02:16.742
- Ooh! You came with the acting!

00:02:16.742 --> 00:02:18.120
I was like different accent!

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:18.953
- Yep!

00:02:18.953 --> 00:02:19.786
(laughing)

00:02:19.786 --> 00:02:20.679
- I was like what? No!

00:02:20.679 --> 00:02:22.010
You're trying shit!

00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:25.183
You're trying rubbish!

00:02:25.183 --> 00:02:28.207
So then, yeah man, it actually happened.

00:02:28.207 --> 00:02:29.440
And then straight after

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:30.439
I called my agent because

00:02:30.439 --> 00:02:31.877
he knew that I was going
to get a phone call.

00:02:31.877 --> 00:02:33.275
And I told him yeah, like,

00:02:33.275 --> 00:02:35.320
"I didn't even get it man."

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:36.317
And my agent was like,

00:02:36.317 --> 00:02:37.840
"Don't worry. It's cool.

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:39.470
Sometimes these things ain't meant to be."

00:02:39.470 --> 00:02:40.633
- Aww, that's so sweet.

00:02:40.633 --> 00:02:41.466
- And I was like,

00:02:41.466 --> 00:02:42.299
"What do you mean?

00:02:42.299 --> 00:02:43.132
Of course we got it!"

00:02:43.132 --> 00:02:44.010
And he got (slang).

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:45.951
That was a blessing.

00:02:45.951 --> 00:02:47.540
I will never forget that day!

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:48.930
Literally, I will never forget it.

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:50.799
- That is so nice!

00:02:50.799 --> 00:02:52.554
I'm so happy for you!

00:02:52.554 --> 00:02:54.277
(mumbling)

00:02:54.277 --> 00:02:56.610
(laughing)

00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:59.050
I saw a video where you took your mom

00:02:59.050 --> 00:03:01.470
to see a Top Boy billboard.

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:03.010
- So you're proper preemie like that?

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:04.499
- As I said, I'm good at my job!

00:03:04.499 --> 00:03:07.001
I wanted to come with the information.

00:03:07.001 --> 00:03:08.500
- That's good!

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:10.298
- What has been your mom's reaction

00:03:10.298 --> 00:03:12.520
to you being in this show.

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:13.800
And all your family and friends.

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:14.810
What's the reaction been

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:16.060
around you getting this opportunity?

00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:17.860
- For me it's like once in a lifetime.

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:19.790
And being able to be a part of it

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:20.807
is just crazy, man.

00:03:20.807 --> 00:03:22.100
And obviously that billboard,

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:23.700
it was just me and Ash up there.

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:25.250
So like, a lot of people,

00:03:25.250 --> 00:03:26.470
if they don't even know you

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:28.850
they know that you are good

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:30.610
or a main character in the thing.

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:32.710
So like, my mom, it's just good for her.

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:34.880
You know, she's got bragging rights now

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:35.927
and stuff like that.

00:03:35.927 --> 00:03:38.900
But it's just, again,
we're just all blessed

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:40.670
and happy that at least

00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:41.732
one of us has been able
to get his opportunity.

00:03:41.732 --> 00:03:43.380
You know what I'm saying?

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:44.590
- So I notice you've been calling

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:45.940
Ashley Walters by Ash.

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:46.773
- Yeah!

00:03:46.773 --> 00:03:47.906
- So you guys are really good friends?

00:03:47.906 --> 00:03:48.757
- Yeah, we're like that now.

00:03:48.757 --> 00:03:49.590
- You're best friends?

00:03:49.590 --> 00:03:50.753
- Yeah, we've been eating dinner.

00:03:50.753 --> 00:03:52.286
- Really?

00:03:52.286 --> 00:03:53.411
- Yo! It's mad.

00:03:53.411 --> 00:03:54.805
- Really? Because I said
hi to Ashley Walters

00:03:54.805 --> 00:03:56.670
and left and he doesn't know me.

00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:57.503
(laughing)

00:03:57.503 --> 00:03:58.667
- So I was like (squeeking sound).

00:03:58.667 --> 00:03:59.500
- You've got to get to know him.

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:00.504
- I know. You're so right.

00:04:00.504 --> 00:04:02.249
You can't just be saying
hi to people like that.

00:04:02.249 --> 00:04:04.440
- Yeah, that's the thing, man.

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:05.273
- Yeah, I don't have any chill

00:04:05.273 --> 00:04:07.530
so I was like, "Hey!"

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:08.910
So tell me about your experience

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:09.950
working with, you know,

00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:11.060
the original cast members.

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:12.000
As you said, you've got Ashley,

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:13.400
you've got Kano,

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:15.007
you've got people like that.

00:04:15.007 --> 00:04:16.853
- Let me say again, surreal.

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:19.546
Ashley's just someone that

00:04:19.546 --> 00:04:20.910
I've looked up to because

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:22.030
he's broken down a barrier

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:23.800
by going down over into the States.

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:24.633
Because I've seen him in

00:04:24.633 --> 00:04:25.466
"Get Rich Or Die Trying"

00:04:25.466 --> 00:04:27.630
and that's one of my favorite movies.

00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:29.650
So seeing him and I was thinking

00:04:29.650 --> 00:04:31.405
he's made this possible.

00:04:31.405 --> 00:04:33.090
He's actually paved the way for

00:04:33.090 --> 00:04:34.850
people like me to come through.

00:04:34.850 --> 00:04:36.491
So I'm always grateful for that.

00:04:36.491 --> 00:04:37.460
(Gena) As someone who's younger

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:38.293
in the industry

00:04:38.293 --> 00:04:39.780
what's he best piece of advice

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:41.360
that you've been given so far

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:42.490
in your career?

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:43.453
- Stay humble.

00:04:45.034 --> 00:04:47.140
- You're definitely doing that.

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:49.430
- Yeah, man. I hear it
all the time as well.

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:51.270
And something I realized

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:53.160
anyway, people can lose their way

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:53.993
and stuff like that

00:04:53.993 --> 00:04:55.588
because of stuff like this.

00:04:55.588 --> 00:04:56.421
You know what I'm saying?

00:04:56.421 --> 00:04:57.650
There's a lot of people that will say yes.

00:04:57.650 --> 00:04:58.483
So yeah, man.

00:04:58.483 --> 00:04:59.780
You've always got to stay humble

00:04:59.780 --> 00:05:01.130
and appreciate everything

00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:02.014
that you have in life.

00:05:02.014 --> 00:05:03.000
(Gena) What other shows

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:04.290
do you watch on Netflix?

00:05:04.290 --> 00:05:06.270
Or have you watched on Netflix?

00:05:06.270 --> 00:05:07.787
- I've recently watched

00:05:07.787 --> 00:05:08.820
"When They See Us".

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:12.302
And that has inspired me so, so much.

00:05:12.302 --> 00:05:13.850
The level of acting.

00:05:13.850 --> 00:05:15.440
The director, Ava,

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:17.520
she done an amazing job.

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:19.220
Even light and sound.

00:05:19.220 --> 00:05:22.100
You really appreciate everything

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:22.933
when it comes to

00:05:22.933 --> 00:05:23.766
"When They See Us".

00:05:23.766 --> 00:05:25.090
It was an amazing show.

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:27.380
And, for me, it's opened my eyes

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:29.220
and yet inspired me to just want to

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:30.594
tell stories now because

00:05:30.594 --> 00:05:32.970
before when people used to ask me,

00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:33.890
"Now that you've got Top Boy

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:34.860
what kind of stuff do you want to do?"

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:35.870
And I obviously I never started

00:05:35.870 --> 00:05:36.870
with acting so

00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:38.660
I'm kind of just going with the flow.

00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:41.070
Just doing roles that I feel like is good.

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:42.380
You know what I'm saying?

00:05:42.380 --> 00:05:43.313
But now I actually know

00:05:43.313 --> 00:05:45.030
that I want to tell really

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:46.794
important stories that need to be told.

00:05:46.794 --> 00:05:49.430
(Gena) Who's someone that you admire?

00:05:49.430 --> 00:05:51.460
- I'd say my uncle.

00:05:51.460 --> 00:05:52.840
I admire him a lot.

00:05:52.840 --> 00:05:54.520
Because I wasn't actually born here.

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:55.880
I was born in Jamaica.

00:05:55.880 --> 00:05:57.400
So I came here when I was four.

00:05:57.400 --> 00:05:58.420
Obviously my dad died

00:05:58.420 --> 00:05:59.540
when I was like two.

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:01.760
So then, yeah like, my uncle

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:03.140
just got us all over.

00:06:03.140 --> 00:06:05.140
Which he never needed to do.

00:06:05.140 --> 00:06:08.030
And also, he's opened
up his own restaurant

00:06:08.030 --> 00:06:09.000
and stuff like that.

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:12.210
So, yeah man, he's mad inspiring or me

00:06:12.210 --> 00:06:13.820
and I just admire him so much.

00:06:13.820 --> 00:06:15.240
Especially just because I'm here.

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:16.650
Because I know I never needed to be here.

00:06:16.650 --> 00:06:18.490
And I see my family in Jamaica

00:06:18.490 --> 00:06:19.334
and I'm just thinking

00:06:19.334 --> 00:06:21.029
that could have been me.

00:06:21.029 --> 00:06:22.940
(Gena) I'm glad you mentioned Jamaica.

00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:23.910
Because you were born in Jamaica.

00:06:23.910 --> 00:06:24.760
I was not born in Jamaica but

00:06:24.760 --> 00:06:26.304
I'm British born Jamaican, okay?

00:06:26.304 --> 00:06:27.707
- You're a jafaker!

00:06:27.707 --> 00:06:28.620
- I'm not a jafaker!

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:29.900
Why do you guys always say that?

00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:32.900
You always try to say that we're jafakans!

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:33.768
- When you're actually from there

00:06:33.768 --> 00:06:35.088
that's the bragging rights you have!

00:06:35.088 --> 00:06:36.000
- All right, but you have been here

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:37.730
since you were four so.

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:38.563
Do you know what I mean?

00:06:38.563 --> 00:06:39.396
Like, don't even try it!

00:06:39.396 --> 00:06:40.229
You're Jamaican,

00:06:40.229 --> 00:06:41.128
I'm half Jamaican.

00:06:41.128 --> 00:06:42.520
Let's say that since

00:06:42.520 --> 00:06:44.941
your trying to deny my whole existence.

00:06:44.941 --> 00:06:46.420
(mumbles)

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:47.900
What's the best thing about

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:48.733
being Jamaican?

00:06:48.733 --> 00:06:50.700
- From such a small island

00:06:50.700 --> 00:06:52.864
the fact that people speak about us is,

00:06:52.864 --> 00:06:56.350
like we're always
constantly in conversations.

00:06:56.350 --> 00:06:57.190
So I feel like that's

00:06:57.190 --> 00:06:58.023
the best thing.

00:06:58.023 --> 00:06:59.930
We're proud of that.

00:06:59.930 --> 00:07:00.763
- It's wild how they've got

00:07:00.763 --> 00:07:01.747
so much culture capital.

00:07:01.747 --> 00:07:02.967
It's such a small island

00:07:02.967 --> 00:07:06.117
but so many people.

00:07:06.117 --> 00:07:07.849
- And a lot of time when people

00:07:07.849 --> 00:07:09.820
refer to the Caribbean

00:07:09.820 --> 00:07:11.740
they are actually talking about Jamaica.

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:12.573
I'm sorry.

00:07:12.573 --> 00:07:14.663
- Which is offensive to
literally every the other island.

00:07:14.663 --> 00:07:15.962
- It's the truth.

00:07:15.962 --> 00:07:18.040
From where I'm from I know that

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:19.620
a lot of the times when you see

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:21.803
when you talk about Africans

00:07:21.803 --> 00:07:23.560
versus Jamaicans,

00:07:23.560 --> 00:07:24.772
well, Carribeans.

00:07:24.772 --> 00:07:26.860
A lot of times it's
Africans versus Jamaicans.

00:07:26.860 --> 00:07:28.971
So that's what I've seen.

00:07:28.971 --> 00:07:30.656
I'm only going off what I've seen.

00:07:30.656 --> 00:07:31.803
Just to clear that up.

00:07:32.758 --> 00:07:34.330
(Gena) So next time I see you,

00:07:34.330 --> 00:07:35.960
if I'm ever lucky enough to see you again,

00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:36.793
right?

00:07:36.793 --> 00:07:37.626
- You will.

00:07:37.626 --> 00:07:38.459
Don't say it like that.

00:07:38.459 --> 00:07:39.292
You will see me again.

00:07:39.292 --> 00:07:40.330
- Because we're friends!

00:07:40.330 --> 00:07:41.180
Top Boy will be out

00:07:41.180 --> 00:07:42.013
in the world.

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:44.630
What are you most excited about

00:07:44.630 --> 00:07:45.740
for the show's release?

00:07:45.740 --> 00:07:47.990
- I'm just excited for people

00:07:47.990 --> 00:07:50.800
to see a UK story

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:52.270
on a worldwide stage.

00:07:52.270 --> 00:07:53.380
- Absolutely.

00:07:53.380 --> 00:07:54.213
- It's going to be mad

00:07:54.213 --> 00:07:55.870
that people from Brazil are

00:07:55.870 --> 00:07:57.580
going to know about this now.

00:07:57.580 --> 00:08:00.010
People from Bangladesh apparently,

00:08:00.010 --> 00:08:01.180
I heard.

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:02.013
Bangladesh?

00:08:02.013 --> 00:08:04.113
(laughing)

00:08:06.115 --> 00:08:08.552
- Worldwide, baby! We're
going international!

00:08:08.552 --> 00:08:09.820
- That's what's up!

00:08:09.820 --> 00:08:10.980
So, yeah man, I'm just excited for

00:08:10.980 --> 00:08:13.370
people to know about our culture,

00:08:13.370 --> 00:08:15.315
how we speak as well.

00:08:15.315 --> 00:08:16.353
(Gena) This was great.

00:08:16.353 --> 00:08:17.290
- Thank you so much for chatting

00:08:17.290 --> 00:08:18.123
with me.

00:08:18.123 --> 00:08:18.956
- It's alright!

00:08:18.956 --> 00:08:21.332
- Michael! Michael Ward,
you're going to be famous!

00:08:21.332 --> 00:08:23.180
And I can't wait to see it and say

00:08:23.180 --> 00:08:24.820
that I spoke to you!

00:08:24.820 --> 00:08:25.910
Make sure you accept,

00:08:25.910 --> 00:08:26.980
when I follow your Instagram

00:08:26.980 --> 00:08:28.890
make sure you're accepting it.

00:08:28.890 --> 00:08:30.923
- Maybe, I don't know about that!

00:08:30.923 --> 00:08:33.590
(hip hop music)

